title: "Removing stars from linear astronomical images with a network trained without any third-party star remover"
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: "Nicolas"
date-released: 2026-11-27
version: "1.0"
license: AGPL-3.0-or-later
repository-code: "https://github.com/n1c1-1/float-star-removal"
abstract: "A NAFNet that splits a linear astronomical image into a starless image and a stars layer, trained on synthetic pairs and on real pairs whose targets come from a published, Gaia-guided classical chain, with a checkable provenance of every training target."
keywords:
  - astronomy
  - star removal
  - image restoration
  - NAFNet
  - Gaia
